> **How large is the operational exposure created by delayed ED-to-speciality transfer, and what portion could plausibly be addressable through coordination automation?**

The critical methodological rule is:

> **Patient waiting time is not staff labour time.**

The AIIMS Bhopal study measures patient-flow delay and classifies causes, but it does not measure staff minutes spent calling, messaging, checking beds, negotiating ownership or escalating cases.

Therefore this checkpoint quantifies:

1. direct patient-flow exposure;
2. exception volume;
3. potential addressable delay using scenario modelling;

but **does not invent labour savings**.

